<header><p class="st-kicker">other · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Confederate Ireland</h1><p class="st-meta">1642 CE – 1652 CE · capital Kilkenny</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Catholic government formed at Kilkenny during the Irish Confederate Wars, which ruled most of Ireland in the 1640s until Cromwell's conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The rebellion of October 1641 by Catholic Irish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a> spread across the island. In 1642 Catholic clergy and lords formed the Confederation of Kilkenny, a government loyal to Charles I but demanding Catholic rights and self-government for Ireland.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A General Assembly and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/supreme-council-of-the-irish-confederation">Supreme Council</a> governed, raising taxes and armies. Its motto was 'Irishmen united for God, King and country'. The papal nuncio Rinuccini divided the Confederates over peace with the king. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owen-roe-oneill">Owen Roe O'Neill</a> won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-benburb">Battle of Benburb</a> in 1646, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-preston-1st-viscount-tara">Thomas Preston</a> led the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a> army.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Confederation dissolved itself in 1649 to ally with the royalists under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-butler-1st-duke-of-ormonde">Ormond</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell">Oliver Cromwell's</a> campaign from 1649 and the surrender of the last Irish forces in 1652 ended it, followed by massive land confiscation under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commonwealth-of-england">Commonwealth of England</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/confederate-ireland.jpg" alt="Confederate Ireland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Raymond1922A · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Green_harp_flag_of_Ireland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1642 CE – 1652 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kilkenny</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Owen Roe O'Neill, Thomas Preston, Richard Bellings</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Irish, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Irish Catholic Confederation, Confederation of Kilkenny</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1647&amp;focus=confederate-ireland" aria-label="Confederate Ireland on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4518 362 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Confederate Ireland lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4838 618L4861 599M4838 618L4997 651"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4861 599h0M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4838 618h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4838 618h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kilkenny. <a href="/atlas?year=1647&amp;focus=confederate-ireland">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
